---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import PageHero from '../components/PageHero.astro';
import DraftBanner from '../components/DraftBanner.astro';
import { site } from '../lib/site';
import { url } from '../lib/url';
---
<Base title="Privacy Policy — New Beginnings Recovery" description="How New Beginnings Recovery collects, uses, shares, and protects your information, and your California privacy rights." phiPage={false}>
  <PageHero eyebrow="Privacy Policy" title="Your privacy, in plain terms" />
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container prose">
      <DraftBanner />
      <p class="updated">Effective date: [to be set at launch]</p>

      <p>This Privacy Policy explains how New Beginnings Recovery (“we,” “us”) collects, uses, discloses, and protects information when you visit newbeginningsrecovery.com (the “Site”). Health information you provide as a patient is also protected under our <a href={url('/notice-of-privacy-practices/')}>Notice of Privacy Practices</a> and, for substance-use-disorder records, under federal law (42 C.F.R. Part 2). Where those apply, they govern that information.</p>

      <h2>Information we collect</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Identifiers &amp; contact data</strong> — name, phone, email, and similar details you submit.</li>
        <li><strong>Insurance information</strong> — provider and member details you share to verify benefits.</li>
        <li><strong>Health / substance-use information</strong> — details you choose to share about treatment needs. This is <strong>sensitive personal information</strong>.</li>
        <li><strong>Internet &amp; usage data</strong> — pages viewed and similar analytics, collected only with your consent (see <a href={url('/privacy-choices/')}>Your Privacy Choices</a>).</li>
        <li><strong>Inferences</strong> drawn from the above to help us respond to your inquiry.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>How we use information</h2>
      <p>To respond to inquiries, verify insurance, provide and improve our services, communicate with you (with your consent), maintain security, and comply with law.</p>

      <h2>How we share information — and your opt-out</h2>
      <p>We do <strong>not</strong> sell your personal information for money. However, when analytics or advertising technologies are enabled with your consent, sharing certain identifiers with those partners for cross-context behavioral advertising may be considered a <strong>“sale” or “share”</strong> under California law. You can opt out at any time through <a href={url('/privacy-choices/')}>Your Privacy Choices</a>, and we honor Global Privacy Control (GPC) browser signals as a valid opt-out. We do not use advertising or analytics trackers on pages where you submit health information.</p>

      <h2>Sensitive personal information</h2>
      <p>We limit our use of sensitive personal information (including health and substance-use information) to what is necessary to provide the services you request. See “Limit the Use of My Sensitive Personal Information” under <a href={url('/privacy-choices/')}>Your Privacy Choices</a>.</p>

      <h2>Your California privacy rights</h2>
      <p>If you are a California resident, you have the right to know, access, correct, and delete your personal information; to opt out of sale/sharing; to limit the use of sensitive personal information; and to not be discriminated against for exercising these rights.</p>
      <p><strong>How to exercise your rights:</strong> submit a request by (1) calling <a href={site.phoneHref}>{site.phone}</a> or (2) emailing <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>. We will verify your identity, respond within 45 days (extendable as allowed by law), and offer an appeal if we decline. An authorized agent may submit a request on your behalf with proof of authorization.</p>

      <h2>Cookies &amp; tracking</h2>
      <p>Non-essential cookies and trackers load only after you opt in, and we honor GPC. Manage your choices any time via <a href={url('/privacy-choices/')}>Your Privacy Choices</a>.</p>

      <h2>Consumer health data</h2>
      <p>For consumer health data covered by state consumer-health-data laws, see our <a href={url('/consumer-health-data/')}>Consumer Health Data Notice</a>.</p>

      <h2>Children</h2>
      <p>The Site is not directed to children under 13, and we do not knowingly collect their personal information.</p>

      <h2>Data retention &amp; security</h2>
      <p>We retain personal information only as long as necessary for the purposes described or as required by law, and we maintain reasonable administrative, technical, and physical safeguards.</p>

      <h2>Changes &amp; contact</h2>
      <p>We may update this policy and will revise the effective date above. Questions? Call <a href={site.phoneHref}>{site.phone}</a> or email <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>. {site.addressLine}.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
